{"step_index":2558,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T11:16:09Z","input_tokens":2943,"cache_read_tokens":56433,"output_tokens":3359,"thinking":"Phase 7 exploration enhances stage navigation. It introduces direct workspace access for unsolved problems via a \"practice-next\" action. Alternative stage exploration is available through filtered problem lists or stage topic opening using a \"explore-problems\" action.\n\n\nThe system uses `localStorage` to manage the active stage, reading and writing the `dsa_active_stage` key. The `DsaDashboard` component handles stage loading and setting through `loadActiveStage()` and `setActiveStage()` methods, respectively. This determines the current stage and its persistence across sessions.\n\n\nStage navigation relies on `localStorage` for active stage persistence. The `DsaDashboard` component handles stage management through its `loadActiveStage()` and `setActiveStage()` methods. These methods use the `dsa_active_stage` key to determine the current stage across sessions, implying its state management is crucial for user experience.\n\n\nPrefix sums offer O(1) range query lookup after O(n) preprocessing; sorting involves comparison-based or linear time complexity with specific invariants. Binary search then efficiently handles monotonic spaces using logarithmic time boundary halving.\n\nLinked lists require heap-allocated node traversal/manipulation; stacks maintain LIFO state, queues FIFO, and deques double-ended FIFO buffers. Pointer redirection, cycle detection, and LIFO stack matching are key.\n\nRecursion and backtracking are essential for problems with overlapping subproblems, requiring structured exploration of all possibilities. This includes problems needing systematic search using recursive strategies.\n\n\nExamining the problem breakdown, recursion and backtracking problems involve building decision trees, defining base cases and exploring choices. Tree traversal methods include preorder, inorder, and postorder for DFS, with BFS using a deque for level-order exploration. Heaps and graph algorithms are also key for algorithmic techniques.\n\n\nStage 8 focuses on graph algorithms, including BFS, DFS, and topological sorting, and also data structures such as Union-Find. Identified the milestone as \"Number of Islands\" and \"Kth Largest Element\", using concepts like adjacency lists and grid traversal. Stage 9 covers Greedy and Dynamic Programming techniques, specifically memoization, tabulation, and interval scheduling. The milestones here are \"Climbing Stairs\" and \"Maximum Subarray\".\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs = require('fs');\\nconst codeProbs = fs.readFileSync('C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_problems.js', 'utf8');\\nconst vm = require('vm');\\nconst sandbox = { window: {} };\\nvm.createContext(sandbox);\\nvm.runInContext(codeProbs, sandbox);\\nconst probs = sandbox.window.DSA_PROBLEMS_LIBRARY;\\nconst byId = new Map();\\nprobs.forEach(p => byId.set(p.id, p));\\n\\nconst stages = [\\n  { stage: 1, milestoneId: 1, starters: [1, 2, 8, 10] },\\n  { stage: 2, milestoneId: 3, starters: [3, 4, 18, 22] },\\n  { stage: 3, milestoneId: 33, starters: [31, 33, 51, 52] },\\n  { stage: 4, milestoneId: 89, starters: [81, 89, 90, 61] },\\n  { stage: 5, milestoneId: 69, starters: [69, 70, 109, 110] },\\n  { stage: 6, milestoneId: 187, starters: [187, 188, 189, 190] },\\n  { stage: 7, milestoneId: 132, starters: [131, 132, 133, 143] },\\n  { stage: 8, milestoneId: 205, starters: [161, 205, 206, 207] },\\n  { stage: 9, milestoneId: 239, starters: [239, 240, 251, 252] },\\n  { stage: 10, milestoneId: 10, starters: [10, 273, 283, 291] }\\n];\\n\\nstages.forEach(s => {\\n  const m = byId.get(s.milestoneId);\\n  console.log('Stage ' + s.stage + ' Milestone:', m ? (m.id + ' - ' + m.title) : 'MISSING');\\n  s.starters.forEach(id => {\\n    const p = byId.get(id);\\n    if (!p) console.log('  MISSING starter ID:', id);\\n    else console.log('  Starter:', p.id, p.title);\\n  });\\n});\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer\"","IsDaemon":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking milestone and starter problem IDs\"","toolSummary":"\"Check milestone and starter problem IDs\""}}]}
