n with pruning to avoid exponential complexity.\n\nStage seven initiates the study of trees and binary search trees.\n\n\nStage seven introduces trees and binary search trees, focusing on traversal algorithms (preorder, inorder, postorder, level-order) and th\n<truncated 1046 bytes>\nes the status of the stage's milestone. It also seems to identify the next unsolved problem and track the difficulty distribution.\n\n\nAnalyzing the completion rules, `status` determination prioritizes meaningful progress. The function increments difficulty counters. A stage is `mastered` only with 100% completion or significant problem-solving (minimum of 5 solved and 50% completion) alongside milestone completion. Otherwise, the status is `in_progress` if any problems were attempted or solved. The stage remains `not_started` if no problems have been attempted or solved.\n\n\nThe system allows flexible stage navigation; any stage can be set as active, regardless of prior stage completion. The `getActiveStage` and `setActiveStage` methods manage the active stage, storing the selection locally and visually highlighting the active stage. The `practiceNextInStage` method opens the next unsolved problem in a selected stage, utilizing stage statistics.\n\nThe `exploreStageProblems` method enables stage-specific problem exploration, offering a filterable problem table by stage. This stage filtering feature refines problem selection. By setting `selectedStage`, the problems table focuses on a specific stage's problems.\n\n\nThe full roadmap view presents a header with overall KPIs and a subtitle. It includes a navigation bar for quick stage jumps, a filter bar for stage status, and a spotlight card for the active stage. The timeline displays individual stage cards, each with a header, active stage indicator, and status badge.\n\n\nThe roadmap overview card displays stage-specific learning elements, including completion stats, core concepts, and curated problems. Stage filtering relies on a `filterProblems()` function that filters the problem set based on the `selectedStage`. The filtering logic accesses `BEGINNER_ROADMAP_10_STAGES` and uses the stage's topics to determine problem inclusion. Problems are included if they have any of the stage's topics, or the stage's topics match the problem's `topic` or `primaryTopic` properties.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js\"","EndLine":"1420","StartLine":"1350","toolAction":"\"Viewing sub-views rendering in dsa_dashboard.js\"","toolSummary":"\"View sub-views rendering in dsa_dashboard.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
